+## Built State (F267, 2026-09-24)
+
+What exists on disk at the close of F267, built in one round of one session on
+`feature/f267-list-commands-v2-completion`, cut from `main` at `9f06c509`. Every DECISION named lives
+in `.agent/decisions.md`; every round's verdict in `.agent/live_review.md` or, once rotated, its
+archive.
+
+**T001 — the wirings.** Landed in F273's round 9 (DECISION F273 D9), before this feature was
+claimed: `test.list`, `mission.list`, `change.list` and `event.list` call `apply_list_options`, each
+with its own tests. F267 changed no production file.
+
+**T002 — the catalog-driven handler test.** `tests/cli/test_list_commands_everywhere.py` takes its
+commands from `_is_list_command` over `CATALOG`, the predicate the catalog itself uses to attach
+the shared flags, so a list command added later joins the test with no edit to it (DECISION F267
+D1). At the claim that predicate selected 13 commands: `blocker.list`, `change.list`,
+`config.list`, `decision.list`, `event.list`, `job.list`, `memory.list`, `mission.list`,
+`patch.list`, `project.list`, `run.list`, `test.list` and `worker.list`. Each one runs through
+`apps.cli.grouped.main`, in a data root holding one registered project and one saved empty job,
+once in text and once under `--json`, and must exit non-zero with the refusal
+`unknown --sort field 'bogus'; valid fields: ` followed by its field names. No command is excluded.
+The four DECISION F262 D4 exclusions are named in the test with their reasons, and the test fails
+if any of them returns to the catalog; it also fails, naming the command, if a list command ever
+requires a positional other than `job_id`.
+
+**T003 — the ten-second demo.** The same file seeds three runs in `run list`'s store, finished five
+days, two days and one hour ago, and runs `remedy run list --since 3d --until 1d` in a child
+process, in JSON and in text: only the run from two days ago comes back.
+
+**Acceptance, by the test that proves it.** `--sort bogus` exits non-zero and names the valid
+fields, for every command in scope: `TestEveryHandlerRefusesAnUnknownSortField`, whose text and
+JSON cases are parametrized over the derived set. `--limit 1` and the time window filtering each
+command's real rows: the per-command tests F262 and F273 landed beside each wiring, for example
+`tests/cli/test_event_list_cmd.py`, `tests/cli/test_change_proof_cli.py` and
+`tests/cli/test_mission_cmd.py`. The catalog-driven set: `TestTheInScopeSet`. The ten-second demo:
+`TestTheTenSecondDemo`. Round 1's mutation proofs turned the handler cases of `change.list`,
+`decision.list`, `mission.list` and `config.list` red when each dropped `--sort`, and the demo red
+when `run list` lost its date or a relative bound pointed forward in time.
+
+**Modules and lists (closure precondition 7).** F267 added no module under `apps/` or `packages/`,
+no line to `tests/orchestration/import_reachability_allowlist.txt`, and nothing to
+`ALLOWED_UNWIRED` or `RESERVED_NAMESPACES` in `tests/test_no_orphan_modules.py`.
+
+**Findings.** F267 registered none. The four open findings at its claim, R-0499, R-0950, R-1008 and
+R-1046, are owned by F284 and were neither touched nor re-assigned.
